From: LioraGuo-wiwynn <liora.guo.wiwynn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Oct 2025 10:20:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] oemcommands: Stabilize motherboard FRU selection on
 AC-off

Task Description:
1) On multi-host platforms, when AC is off the entity-manager
   removes parts of the inventory. As a result, the number of objects
   under xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.Board.Motherboard shrinks.
   Our previous index-based selection then "shifts" (later objects move
   forward), causing the wrong motherboard FRU to be selected and shown.
2) Reduces unnecessary DBus traversal

Motivation:
Index-based selection assumes a stable ordering and a complete list
of motherboard objects. When inventory entries disappear (AC off),
indices no longer correspond to the original host positions.

Design:
1) Replace index-based selection with a predicate-based lookup:
   - For multi-host platforms with hostPosition > 0, select the path
     whose name contains the suffix `_<hostPosition>` or
     `_Slot_<hostPosition>`.
   - Otherwise default to the first match.
     This keeps selection stable even when the list shrinks.

2) In getFruData(), if getMotherBoardFruPath() returns a non-empty
   path, read the Asset decorator properties (e.g., SN/PN) directly
   from that object and return early.

